# Implementation plan — Spec 1.9.4

## Summary

Post-login **session role selection** for users with multiple platform roles. Extends `@webonone/platform-nav` with `companyAdmin` and `member` variants; WebOnOne frontend dialog + Redux session state; backend assumable-roles API and session-aware email sync. See [02-session-role-selection.md](./02-session-role-selection.md), [03-nav-and-permissions.md](./03-nav-and-permissions.md), [04-email-role-handoff.md](./04-email-role-handoff.md).

## Branch and prerequisites

| Item | Value |
|------|--------|
| Branch | `spec/1.9.4` |
| Package builds | `npm run build -w @webonone/platform-nav` before WebOnOne prod build |
| Depends on | Spec 1.9.3 `users_roles` migration applied |
| Super admin seed | `SUPER_ADMIN_USER_ID` in `webonone-v2/backend/.env` |

---

## Phase 1 — Platform nav variants

**Goal:** Nav defs for company admin and member (no Email).

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| Extend `PlatformNavVariant` | `packages/platform-nav/src/coreNav.ts` |
| Add `COMPANY_ADMIN_PLATFORM_NAV`, `MEMBER_PLATFORM_NAV` | same |
| Add `CORE_NAV_VARIANT_COMPANY_ADMIN`, update parsers | same |
| Re-export types | `packages/platform-nav/src/index.ts` |

**Exit criteria:** `companyAdmin` shows Email; `member` omits Email group.

**Verify:** `npm run build -w @webonone/platform-nav`

---

## Phase 2 — Backend assumable roles + session sync

**Goal:** Role picker API and validated email sync.

| Task | Paths |
|------|-------|
| `getAssumableRoles(userId)` | `webonone-v2/backend/src/services/company.service.ts` |
| Repository helpers | `webonone-v2/backend/src/repositories/userRole.repository.ts` |
| `GET /company/me/assumable-roles` | `company.routes.ts`, `company.controller.ts` |
| Sync body schema | `webonone-v2/backend/src/schemas/` (Zod) |
| Session-aware `syncEmailRoleForUser` | `company.service.ts` — validate requested role against `users_roles` |

**Exit criteria:** API returns roles list; sync respects `sessionRole` body.

**Verify:** `npm run type-check -w @webonone/webonone-backend`

